  "steps": [
    "Place 1 cup (90 g) rolled oats into a high-speed blender and pulse on high for 10 to 15 seconds until finely ground into flour consistency.",
    "Add 1 cup (226 g) cottage cheese, 3 large eggs, 1 tsp baking powder, 1/2 tsp vanilla extract, 1/4 tsp ground cinnamon, and 1/8 tsp salt to the blender. Blend on medium-high speed for 20 to 30 seconds until completely smooth and batter thickens.",
    "Melt 1 tsp butter in a large nonstick skillet or griddle set over medium heat for 2 minutes until hot and shimmering.",
    "Pour batter into skillet to form 4-inch pancakes (roughly 1/4 cup per pancake). Cook over medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes until tiny bubbles pop on the surface and edges look golden brown and set.",
    "Flip carefully with a spatula and cook the second side for 1 to 2 minutes until light brown and springy to the touch in the center. Repeat with any remaining batter."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Blend the oats first into flour before adding liquid ingredients to ensure a completely smooth pancake texture.",
    "Keep heat at medium or medium-low so the cottage cheese melts evenly without burning the pancake exterior.",
    "Freeze cooked, cooled pancakes in a single layer, then transfer to a freezer bag; reheat directly in a toaster."
  ],
  "storage": "Store leftover pancakes in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days, or freeze for up to 1 month.",
  "tools": [
